# kk: KK_WORKAROUND_14 only on multiplications with a constant
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45953 state=closed
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

The Apple compiler does not correctly handle multiplications with
NaN * 0 when the 0 is written as a constant: it gives 0 instead of
NaN. Before, KK_WORKAROUND_14 was applied to all multiplications. Now
only to multiplications with a constant (fmul and flrp in
nir_to_msl.c).

* CTS: 5,931 float_controls2 tests. With this change, 0 failures. With
  KK_WORKAROUND_14 disabled, 24 failures (reflect/refract with NaN),
  which shows the tests catch the error and this change still avoids
  it.
* Hardware: M5 Pro, macOS 27.2.
* Performance: in a heavy game in a PS5 emulator, the GPU takes 4.7%
  less time per frame, with 3.7% more frames presented.

Assisted-by: LLM
Original Language: ESP
